expected_issues.description:
If `options.stdin` is an empty string, this branch won’t run, and stdin won’t be closed. Prefer checking `options.stdin !== undefined` so callers can intentionally send empty input and still close stdin to avoid child waiting for EOF.

```suggestion
    if (options.stdin !== undefined) {
      child.stdin!.write(options.stdin);
      child.stdin!.end();
    }
```

